schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Toucan accounts for ~85% of digital carbon-credit volume"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Toucan now accounts for roughly 85% of all digital carbon credits and
    has supported around $4 billion in trading volume, working alongside
    established standards bodies like Gold Standard and Puro.earth.
  evidence: >-
    Stated directly in the source article as a scale figure for Toucan
    Protocol, without an inline citation to a specific report or dashboard.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/what-is-refi.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used by the article to establish Toucan as the dominant infrastructure
    for carbon-credit tokenization before pivoting to the Verra
    retired-credit controversy — i.e. scale is presented alongside a caution
    about quality, not as an unqualified endorsement.
  uncertainty: >-
    No primary source or date-stamped figure is cited in the article for the
    85% / $4B numbers; not independently verified here. Carbon-market
    volume figures are also known to shift quickly and to be reported
    inconsistently across trackers.
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-refi.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
